257
00:11:53,129 --> 00:11:55,589
Good lung sliding, no pneumo.

258
00:11:55,673 --> 00:11:57,091
It is displacement.

259
00:11:57,175 --> 00:11:59,636
Okay, that is a transected trachea.

260
00:12:01,638 --> 00:12:03,639
Pulling out.

261
00:12:03,723 --> 00:12:05,141
Bag.

262
00:12:05,225 --> 00:12:06,684
But if you intubate again,
won't it just come straight

263
00:12:06,768 --> 00:12:08,144
- out the wound?
- Yep, exactly.

264
00:12:08,228 --> 00:12:09,562
So we're gonna need another plan.

265
00:12:09,646 --> 00:12:11,272
Okay. Sats down to 83.

266
00:12:11,356 --> 00:12:12,806
Yeah, he's not moving any air.

267
00:12:12,857 --> 00:12:14,692
Okay, I need a neonatal mask.

268
00:12:14,776 --> 00:12:17,194
- Neonatal?
- Yep.

269
00:12:17,278 --> 00:12:19,697
I'm just going to finish my initial exam.

270
00:12:19,781 --> 00:12:21,950
Let me know if you feel any pain, okay?

271
00:12:25,745 --> 00:12:28,372
My legs are fine.

272
00:12:28,456 --> 00:12:29,999
All looks good.

273
00:12:30,083 --> 00:12:32,543
No need for X-rays or advanced imaging.

274
00:12:32,627 --> 00:12:33,961
Got it.

275
00:12:34,045 --> 00:12:36,545
- Two areas of ecchymosis...
- That means bruising.

276
00:12:36,589 --> 00:12:38,174
Over the shoulders bilaterally.

277
00:12:38,258 --> 00:12:39,884
- I'll document with photos.
- Okay.

278
00:12:39,968 --> 00:12:42,011
Dana will finish up her work,
and I will be in the ER

279
00:12:42,095 --> 00:12:43,721
if you have any questions.

280
00:12:43,805 --> 00:12:45,306
You're in great hands.

281
00:12:45,390 --> 00:12:47,892
Thank you.

282
00:12:47,976 --> 00:12:50,227
All right, Ilana.

283
00:12:50,311 --> 00:12:52,188
I read your intake.

284
00:12:52,272 --> 00:12:53,564
Why don't you give me your description

285
00:12:53,648 --> 00:12:55,191
of exactly what happened?

286
00:12:58,069 --> 00:13:02,114
I was at a 4th of July barbecue

287
00:13:02,198 --> 00:13:04,950
with a bunch of friends.

288
00:13:05,034 --> 00:13:07,745
I helped set up.

289
00:13:15,128 --> 00:13:16,587
Where does it hurt?

290
00:13:16,671 --> 00:13:20,049
<i>Like here, under my belly button.</i>

291
00:13:20,133 --> 00:13:23,427
Okay, do you have any fever,
vomiting, diarrhea?

292
00:13:23,511 --> 00:13:26,847
<i>Oh, no.
It's--it's just a stomachache.</i>

293
00:13:26,931 --> 00:13:29,141
Okay, well, still, go see
the nurse and have her call me.

294
00:13:29,225 --> 00:13:30,601
<i>Okay.</i>

295
00:13:30,685 --> 00:13:33,062
<i>But I'm still having ice cream tonight.</i>

296
00:13:33,146 --> 00:13:35,231
Why don't you see how you feel later?

297
00:13:35,315 --> 00:13:38,776
<i>It--it's not bad.
You don't have to get so sad.</i>

298
00:13:38,860 --> 00:13:41,153
- I'm not sad. I'm--
- I'm good.

299
00:13:41,237 --> 00:13:43,489
<i>Your face doesn't look good.</i>

300
00:13:43,573 --> 00:13:44,907
Oh.

301
00:13:44,991 --> 00:13:46,992
Well, you still wanna watch
the fireworks tonight?

302
00:13:47,076 --> 00:13:48,369
I have our headphones--

303
00:13:49,996 --> 00:13:52,457
- I'm not being rude.
- Sorry, Becca. I gotta go.

304
00:13:58,463 --> 00:14:01,757
Elliot Green, 17, syncopal
episode at football practice.

305
00:14:01,841 --> 00:14:03,634
Look, I just got dizzy, okay?

306
00:14:03,718 --> 00:14:05,219
It's hell week.
I need to get back.

307
00:14:05,303 --> 00:14:06,971
Yeah, okay, tough guy.

308
00:14:07,055 --> 00:14:10,975
A and O, systolic of 95, tachy
at 122, no meds, no allergies.

309
00:14:11,059 --> 00:14:12,509
How long were you at practice?

310
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:14,979
I started at 9:00, so, like, four hours.

311
00:14:15,063 --> 00:14:17,439
Four hours in this heat with all that gear?

312
00:14:17,523 --> 00:14:19,650
No pain, no game.

313
00:14:21,611 --> 00:14:24,155
God, I'm hungry.

314
00:14:25,698 --> 00:14:28,993
Hey. When's our break?
There's no breaks down here.

315
00:14:29,077 --> 00:14:32,037
Always make sure you pack
a protein bar, something quick.

316
00:14:32,121 --> 00:14:35,958
Ogilvie, Joy, jump in on this.

317
00:14:36,042 --> 00:14:37,492
Syncope at football practice.

318
00:14:37,543 --> 00:14:40,629
No, I just--
I just needed to hydrate.

319
00:14:40,713 --> 00:14:42,006
Possible heatstroke?

320
00:14:42,090 --> 00:14:43,257
Well, with heatstroke, you would have

321
00:14:43,341 --> 00:14:44,633
an altered mental status.

322
00:14:44,717 --> 00:14:46,135
And they're usually dry, not sweaty.

323
00:14:46,219 --> 00:14:48,012
Mortality is 50%, especially in the elderly.

324
00:14:48,096 --> 00:14:50,348
In extreme heat like this...

325
00:14:51,391 --> 00:14:52,791
Langdon, can you cover this?

326
00:14:52,850 --> 00:14:55,269
- No problem.
- Mr. Diaz. Orlando.

327
00:14:55,353 --> 00:14:57,146
Orlando, where are you going?

328
00:14:57,230 --> 00:14:58,981
- Home. Can you take these out?
- Uh, no.

329
00:14:59,065 --> 00:15:01,108
It takes 48 hours for you to get out of DKA.

330
00:15:01,192 --> 00:15:02,901
Your blood is still full of acid.

331
00:15:02,985 --> 00:15:04,486
Look, I can't add thousands of dollars

332
00:15:04,570 --> 00:15:05,779
to the 100 grand I already owe.

333
00:15:05,863 --> 00:15:07,698
- I'm--
- I'm sorry. 100 grand?

334
00:15:07,782 --> 00:15:09,950
In medical debt.
My wife doesn't even know.

335
00:15:10,034 --> 00:15:11,952
I'll never be able to pay it off as it is.

336
00:15:12,036 --> 00:15:13,162
Where are your wife and daughter?

337
00:15:13,246 --> 00:15:14,621
Maybe we can all talk.

338
00:15:14,705 --> 00:15:16,206
I told them to go back
to work a couple hours ago.

339
00:15:16,290 --> 00:15:17,875
But the hospital is
giving you a big discount.

340
00:15:17,959 --> 00:15:19,668
And, Mr. Diaz,
I know it's not ideal,

341
00:15:19,752 --> 00:15:21,420
but can you stay for at least 12 hours?

342
00:15:21,504 --> 00:15:23,130
It would get you out of the danger zone.

343
00:15:23,214 --> 00:15:25,716
No. I really can't.

344
00:15:25,800 --> 00:15:29,178
Every minute I stay is a meal,
shoes, school supplies.

345
00:15:29,262 --> 00:15:31,762
Plus, I have a second job
I have to get to by 4:00.

346
00:15:31,764 --> 00:15:34,600
- You need fluids!
- I drink plenty of water.

347
00:15:34,684 --> 00:15:37,034
And potassium and insulin.
Okay, how about this?

348
00:15:37,061 --> 00:15:39,730
You stay and I'll get together
everything you'll need at home.

349
00:15:39,814 --> 00:15:44,068
Also, a referral to Northside
Christian Health Center.

350
00:15:44,152 --> 00:15:46,445
Come on.
You don't work until 4:00.

351
00:15:46,529 --> 00:15:49,156
It'll keep you from passing out
on the job again--

352
00:15:49,240 --> 00:15:50,491
Or worse.

353
00:15:54,454 --> 00:15:55,913
Okay, I guess.

354
00:15:55,997 --> 00:15:57,081
Great.

355
00:15:57,165 --> 00:15:59,000
Thank you. Please.

356
00:16:02,378 --> 00:16:03,879
Sats up to 98.

357
00:16:03,963 --> 00:16:06,632
- Neonatal mask is working.
- Santos, finish the FAST.

358
00:16:06,716 --> 00:16:07,925
What--what are you injecting?

359
00:16:08,009 --> 00:16:09,176
Lido with epi.

360
00:16:09,260 --> 00:16:10,677
It'll clamp off any little bleeders.

361
00:16:10,761 --> 00:16:12,179
We need some skin hooks.
Four Shiley?

362
00:16:12,263 --> 00:16:14,556
Mm, I don't like the curve of a Shiley.

363
00:16:14,640 --> 00:16:16,225
I didn't know you were so picky.

364
00:16:16,309 --> 00:16:17,359
Santos, take a break.

365
00:16:17,393 --> 00:16:19,436
Help me cut down a 6-0 ET tube.

366
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:20,854
What is going on here?

367
00:16:20,938 --> 00:16:22,564
You have a field medic assisting you?

368
00:16:22,648 --> 00:16:23,948
Dr. Abbot is an attending,

369
00:16:24,025 --> 00:16:25,484
and he's also a SWAT physician.

370
00:16:25,568 --> 00:16:28,654
My buddy Hiro here
is in bad need of an airway.

371
00:16:28,738 --> 00:16:30,030
- Cut it right here.
- We can do this.

372
00:16:30,114 --> 00:16:31,281
No, no, I got it.

373
00:16:31,365 --> 00:16:32,408
You must be Gloria's new hire.

374
00:16:32,492 --> 00:16:33,909
Yes. Dr. Al-Hashimi.

375
00:16:33,993 --> 00:16:36,036
Well, I'd shake your hand,
but my tube is ready.

376
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:37,830
And if I could find
and secure the distal trachea,

377
00:16:37,914 --> 00:16:39,164
we have a shot at this.

378
00:16:39,248 --> 00:16:41,625
Okay, keeping an eye on the sats.

379
00:16:41,709 --> 00:16:43,752
Slow is smooth.
Smooth is fast.

380
00:16:43,836 --> 00:16:46,130
You know, you can call me
just to say hi sometimes.

381
00:16:46,214 --> 00:16:47,423
What's up now?

382
00:16:47,507 --> 00:16:48,966
GSW with tracheal transection.

383
00:16:49,050 --> 00:16:52,344
Very retracted, but I think I can get it.

384
00:16:52,428 --> 00:16:54,096
Both lungs are up?

385
00:16:54,180 --> 00:16:56,473
- Sats down to 91.
- Scanning the belly now.

386
00:16:56,557 --> 00:16:58,059
Okay.

387
00:16:59,602 --> 00:17:01,354
I got it. I got it.

388
00:17:04,273 --> 00:17:06,191
Gently, gently, or we're gonna lose it.

389
00:17:06,275 --> 00:17:08,026
Down to 89.

390
00:17:08,110 --> 00:17:09,194
Oh, no.

391
00:17:09,278 --> 00:17:11,239
I'm in. Balloon up.

392
00:17:13,157 --> 00:17:15,784
End tidal, excellent wave form.

393
00:17:15,868 --> 00:17:17,953
Good breath sounds.

394
00:17:18,037 --> 00:17:21,457
I'll sew the tracheal to the skin, 2-0 silk.

395
00:17:21,541 --> 00:17:23,167
- Sats are coming up.
- Whoo.

396
00:17:23,251 --> 00:17:25,627
Not bad, Abbot.

397
00:17:25,711 --> 00:17:27,754
Mm, while you were playing with that airway,

398
00:17:27,838 --> 00:17:29,840
you missed a big bruise
in the left upper quadrant.

399
00:17:29,924 --> 00:17:31,258
He was wearing body armor.

400
00:17:31,342 --> 00:17:32,509
High-velocity projectile doesn't have

401
00:17:32,593 --> 00:17:34,553
to penetrate to damage.

402
00:17:34,637 --> 00:17:37,014
There's no fluid in the suprasplenic space.

403
00:17:37,098 --> 00:17:39,224
Let me look.

404
00:17:39,308 --> 00:17:40,518
Okay, right there.

405
00:17:42,812 --> 00:17:45,162
Looks like a subcapsular
hematoma of his spleen.

406
00:17:45,189 --> 00:17:46,648
Must have been a big impact.

407
00:17:46,732 --> 00:17:49,568
AR-15 muzzle velocity
is 3,000 feet per second.

408
00:17:49,652 --> 00:17:51,069
CT angio of the neck ASAP,

409
00:17:51,153 --> 00:17:53,697
along with CT chest, abdomen, pelvis.

410
00:17:53,781 --> 00:17:56,951
Yep, just as soon as we secure this tube.

411
00:18:00,496 --> 00:18:02,998
- First liter's in.
- Mucous membranes dry.

412
00:18:03,082 --> 00:18:05,209
Pupils four millimeters reactive.

413
00:18:05,293 --> 00:18:06,593
Did you get tackled today?

414
00:18:06,669 --> 00:18:08,003
No, just running drills.

415
00:18:08,087 --> 00:18:09,922
Any chest pain?
Palpitations?

416
00:18:10,006 --> 00:18:11,256
No.

417
00:18:11,340 --> 00:18:12,633
Hands off, please, running the 12 lead.

418
00:18:12,717 --> 00:18:14,134
How are we looking?

419
00:18:14,218 --> 00:18:15,761
Good. Healthy kid.

420
00:18:15,845 --> 00:18:17,262
No history, no trauma.

421
00:18:17,346 --> 00:18:20,224
Differential for syncope in an adolescent?

422
00:18:20,308 --> 00:18:22,351
Cardiac arrhythmia from drugs...

423
00:18:22,435 --> 00:18:23,602
- Hypovolemia, seizure...
- Long QT, WPW...

424
00:18:23,686 --> 00:18:25,229
- Sepsis.
- Or Brugada.

425
00:18:25,313 --> 00:18:27,523
Uh, Brugada is more common in Asian males.

426
00:18:27,607 --> 00:18:29,107
But still should be considered.

427
00:18:29,108 --> 00:18:30,526
Long odds, though.

428
00:18:30,610 --> 00:18:32,444
Brugada prevalence is
one in 20,000 in North America,

429
00:18:32,528 --> 00:18:35,280
as high as one in 300 in Asia
and the Middle East.

430
00:18:35,364 --> 00:18:36,615
And?

431
00:18:36,699 --> 00:18:38,784
First described in 1992, has a high incidence

432
00:18:38,868 --> 00:18:40,661
of sudden death among
young patients with otherwise

433
00:18:40,745 --> 00:18:43,163
- structurally normal hearts--
- Oof, oof, wait.

434
00:18:43,247 --> 00:18:44,797
Did you just say "sudden death"?

435
00:18:44,874 --> 00:18:46,250
Temp is 102.5.

436
00:18:46,334 --> 00:18:47,668
Sorry, our student doctors are discussing

437
00:18:47,752 --> 00:18:50,170
a rare condition you don't have.

438
00:18:50,254 --> 00:18:53,382
I--I just didn't drink enough water.

439
00:18:53,466 --> 00:18:56,385
I overheated.

440
00:18:56,469 --> 00:18:57,928
Not my type, bud.

441
00:18:58,012 --> 00:19:01,182
Other than standard labs, what else to order?

442
00:19:04,644 --> 00:19:06,436
CK to rule out rhabdo.

443
00:19:06,520 --> 00:19:07,688
To make sure you don't have

444
00:19:07,772 --> 00:19:09,231
any muscle breakdown from the heat.

445
00:19:09,315 --> 00:19:11,316
Let's set up a cooling room for Elliot here

446
00:19:11,400 --> 00:19:14,695
and the other heat exhaustions
we'll inevitably get today.

447
00:19:18,407 --> 00:19:20,034
Last photo.

448
00:19:24,038 --> 00:19:25,122
Okay.

449
00:19:25,206 --> 00:19:27,374
We'll take the SD card and seal it

450
00:19:27,458 --> 00:19:30,669
in an evidence envelope with everything else.

451
00:19:30,753 --> 00:19:32,045
Okay.

452
00:19:32,129 --> 00:19:36,008
Next, Emma's gonna turn off the light,

453
00:19:36,092 --> 00:19:38,510
and I'll run a blue light over your skin.

454
00:19:38,594 --> 00:19:44,141
Anything glows, I'll swab it
with a wet, then dry Q-tip.

455
00:19:44,225 --> 00:19:45,392
Is that okay?

456
00:19:45,476 --> 00:19:46,602
Yeah, sure.

457
00:19:49,063 --> 00:19:50,230
All right.

458
00:19:50,314 --> 00:19:52,357
Take off your gown on the left side

459
00:19:52,441 --> 00:19:55,111
and turn a little bit
towards me, just to the left.

460
00:19:57,071 --> 00:19:58,489
There.

461
00:20:23,097 --> 00:20:24,681
Something on the left wrist.

462
00:20:24,765 --> 00:20:25,933
Swab.

463
00:20:33,315 --> 00:20:34,274
Sorry.

464
00:20:34,358 --> 00:20:35,609
Don't be.

465
00:20:35,693 --> 00:20:37,402
- It's just cold.
- Yeah.

466
00:20:37,486 --> 00:20:39,238
Almost done.

467
00:20:45,494 --> 00:20:47,746
- Thanks, Antoine.
- No problem.

468
00:20:47,830 --> 00:20:49,373
Keep your head down out there.

469
00:20:49,457 --> 00:20:50,916
What's the story?

470
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:52,501
Neck angio is negative, missed the carotids.

471
00:20:52,585 --> 00:20:54,294
- He's lucky.
- What about the belly?

472
00:20:54,378 --> 00:20:57,172
Small splenic injury,
no free fluid in the abdomen.

473
00:20:57,256 --> 00:20:59,049
- That should heal on its own.
- What's the plan?

474
00:20:59,133 --> 00:21:00,509
Head and Neck will have an OR ready

475
00:21:00,593 --> 00:21:01,893
with thoracic standing by.

476
00:21:01,927 --> 00:21:03,553
How soon can they take him?

477
00:21:03,637 --> 00:21:05,097
We're a little backed up
with Westbridge patients,

478
00:21:05,181 --> 00:21:06,348
but let's bring him up.

479
00:21:06,432 --> 00:21:08,850
I'll get him taken care of for you.

480
00:21:08,934 --> 00:21:10,477
Hey.

481
00:21:10,561 --> 00:21:13,605
You're gonna be okay, Hiro.
We're getting you to surgery.

482
00:21:13,689 --> 00:21:14,773
I'll write the procedure note.

483
00:21:14,857 --> 00:21:15,983
Thank you.

484
00:21:20,988 --> 00:21:22,030
SWAT? Really?

485
00:21:22,114 --> 00:21:24,032
I suck at golf.

486
00:21:24,116 --> 00:21:26,368
You spend time in the Middle East?

487
00:21:26,452 --> 00:21:27,953
More than I would have liked.

488
00:21:28,037 --> 00:21:30,789
I worked in Kabul
with Médecins Sans Frontières

489
00:21:30,873 --> 00:21:33,542
and in 2020, at the maternity hospital.

490
00:21:33,626 --> 00:21:37,337
I met the most incredible,
bravest doctors there.

491
00:21:37,421 --> 00:21:39,673
Dasht-e-Barchi.

492
00:21:39,757 --> 00:21:42,217
Tragedy.

493
00:21:42,301 --> 00:21:45,470
We should grab a beer sometime,
share war stories.

494
00:21:45,554 --> 00:21:47,640
I'd like that.

495
00:21:50,643 --> 00:21:51,560
She seems cool.

496
00:21:51,644 --> 00:21:53,145
Yep, maybe.

497
00:21:53,229 --> 00:21:56,857
I'm not gonna be around
long enough to find out.

498
00:21:56,941 --> 00:21:59,109
Oh, there she is! Vic!

499
00:21:59,193 --> 00:22:00,277
Dad!

500
00:22:00,361 --> 00:22:03,572
Victoria, this is Dr. Amy Joon.

501
00:22:03,656 --> 00:22:05,407
Dr. Joon is the smartest person I know.

502
00:22:05,491 --> 00:22:07,291
Don't tell your mother.
Just kidding.

503
00:22:08,244 --> 00:22:09,202
But seriously, don't.

504
00:22:09,286 --> 00:22:10,537
- Hi.
- Hello.

505
00:22:10,621 --> 00:22:12,706
Are--are you here to see a patient?

506
00:22:12,790 --> 00:22:14,332
No.
We're here to see you.

507
00:22:14,416 --> 00:22:15,709
Dr. Joon is Chief of Dermatology.

508
00:22:15,793 --> 00:22:17,294
And Victoria's first shift in the ER

509
00:22:17,378 --> 00:22:20,172
was on the day of the PittFest shooting.

510
00:22:20,256 --> 00:22:22,257
I heard all the incredible stories,

511
00:22:22,341 --> 00:22:26,178
including your own acts
of med student prowess.

512
00:22:26,262 --> 00:22:27,929
Wow, med student prowess.

513
00:22:28,013 --> 00:22:30,056
- That's-- I'm--
- I'm pretty sure

514
00:22:30,140 --> 00:22:31,641
I was just trying to stay out of the way.

515
00:22:31,725 --> 00:22:32,976
Ah, she's modest, like her dad.

516
00:22:33,060 --> 00:22:34,811
And her mother?

517
00:22:34,895 --> 00:22:37,022
Oh. Sorry.

518
00:22:37,106 --> 00:22:38,815
Dr. Joon.

519
00:22:38,899 --> 00:22:40,692
Yep, coming.

520
00:22:40,776 --> 00:22:42,819
I'm doing a favor for someone
at the mayor's office

521
00:22:42,903 --> 00:22:45,781
who needs Mohs surgery
on a basal cell carcinoma.

522
00:22:45,865 --> 00:22:47,741
And then I am grilling for 30.

523
00:22:47,825 --> 00:22:49,743
- Oh, wow.
- Happy 4th, all.

524
00:22:49,827 --> 00:22:51,036
- Happy 4th.
- Yeah.

525
00:22:51,120 --> 00:22:53,246
- Thanks for coming down.
- My pleasure.

526
00:22:53,330 --> 00:22:55,457
- Let's grab a coffee sometime.
- Absolutely. Yes.

527
00:22:55,541 --> 00:22:57,793
Thank you.

528
00:22:57,877 --> 00:23:00,337
You know Mom really wants me
to go into surgery.

529
00:23:00,421 --> 00:23:02,172
Ah, your mom wants me to stop drinking

530
00:23:02,256 --> 00:23:04,633
- and join a pickleball league.
- Oh, that's the same.

531
00:23:04,717 --> 00:23:06,259
- Yeah, well--
- Exact same.

532
00:23:06,343 --> 00:23:08,637
I will risk an Achilles tear
before I give up scotch.

533
00:23:08,721 --> 00:23:10,722
Hey, I hope I didn't
embarrass you coming down here.

534
00:23:10,806 --> 00:23:12,140
No.

535
00:23:12,224 --> 00:23:13,934
I'm just trying to present
you with some options

536
00:23:14,018 --> 00:23:15,393
for your residency.

537
00:23:15,477 --> 00:23:17,479
I--I really appreciate it, Dad.

538
00:23:17,563 --> 00:23:19,648
I do.
I just--

539
00:23:19,732 --> 00:23:21,775
I'm still not sure.

540
00:23:21,859 --> 00:23:23,527
Well, either way, you'll do what's right.

541
00:23:23,611 --> 00:23:24,861
You always do.

542
00:23:24,945 --> 00:23:26,780
- Proud of ya.
- Okay.

543
00:23:26,864 --> 00:23:29,366
Dr. Javadi, you are a man of many talents.

544
00:23:29,450 --> 00:23:31,159
You don't know the half of it.

545
00:23:31,243 --> 00:23:32,343
Your daughter has some

546
00:23:32,411 --> 00:23:33,912
high standards to live up to.

547
00:23:33,996 --> 00:23:36,707
Oh, you don't know the half of it.

548
00:23:39,627 --> 00:23:42,963
Mr. and Mrs. Davis, this is
Dr. Jefferson from Psychiatry.

549
00:23:43,047 --> 00:23:44,840
Please call me Caleb.

550
00:23:44,924 --> 00:23:47,259
Can you tell us what's going on with our son?

551
00:23:47,343 --> 00:23:51,096
All of his labs and X-rays came back normal.

552
00:23:51,180 --> 00:23:54,766
Given his age and his hearing voices,

553
00:23:54,850 --> 00:23:59,479
do either of you have a family
history of mental illness?

554
00:23:59,563 --> 00:24:00,981
Not mine.

555
00:24:07,821 --> 00:24:09,406
My brother took his own life.

556
00:24:09,490 --> 00:24:11,783
Wait, what?

557
00:24:11,867 --> 00:24:13,994
Uncle Ken?

558
00:24:14,078 --> 00:24:15,871
You said he drank himself to death.

559
00:24:15,955 --> 00:24:17,706
- Ma.
- He did that too.

560
00:24:17,790 --> 00:24:18,999
Was he ever formally diagnosed

561
