- Jada.
- Excuse me.

570
00:24:37,184 --> 00:24:38,268
Jada.

571
00:24:45,818 --> 00:24:47,611
What happens next?

572
00:24:47,695 --> 00:24:50,030
We keep your son here for the next three days

573
00:24:50,114 --> 00:24:52,032
for observation and therapy.

574
00:24:52,116 --> 00:24:54,716
And that will help us
to understand what is going on.

575
00:24:54,743 --> 00:24:56,193
Jada should really hear this.

576
00:24:56,245 --> 00:24:59,039
Let me see if I can find her, bring her back.

577
00:25:01,709 --> 00:25:04,127
Okay.
I'm gonna swab your mouth now.

578
00:25:04,211 --> 00:25:05,837
My mouth?

579
00:25:05,921 --> 00:25:09,841
Two dry swabs along the inside of your cheek

580
00:25:09,925 --> 00:25:11,969
and then along the gum line.

581
00:25:15,681 --> 00:25:17,641
How you feeling?

582
00:25:19,309 --> 00:25:21,227
I wish this day never happened.

583
00:25:21,311 --> 00:25:23,271
Would you like some medicine
to help you relax?

584
00:25:23,355 --> 00:25:25,524
You've experienced a horrific trauma.

585
00:25:28,027 --> 00:25:29,861
You've been doing this a while?

586
00:25:29,945 --> 00:25:31,363
Let's just say
Florence Nightingale

587
00:25:31,447 --> 00:25:33,365
and I were roommates.

588
00:25:33,449 --> 00:25:35,909
Who?

589
00:25:35,993 --> 00:25:37,452
I rest my case.

590
00:25:37,536 --> 00:25:39,788
She was the founder of modern nursing.

591
00:25:41,707 --> 00:25:44,000
Okay, you can have something
to eat or drink now.

592
00:25:44,084 --> 00:25:46,044
- I'm fine.
- Are you sure?

593
00:25:46,128 --> 00:25:47,837
I'll just keep going.

594
00:25:47,921 --> 00:25:49,882
Okay.

595
00:25:56,597 --> 00:26:01,309
We now have a heat exhaustion
treatment area in North five.

596
00:26:01,393 --> 00:26:03,812
Evaporated cooling.
Great plan.

597
00:26:03,896 --> 00:26:08,525
Yeah, it was
Dr. Langdon's idea.

598
00:26:08,609 --> 00:26:12,445
He figured we'd be seeing a lot
more patients in this heat.

599
00:26:12,529 --> 00:26:14,197
He's right.

600
00:26:14,281 --> 00:26:15,407
How are you feeling?

601
00:26:15,491 --> 00:26:17,909
That's a loaded question.

602
00:26:17,993 --> 00:26:19,953
It wasn't meant to be.

603
00:26:20,037 --> 00:26:22,205
You have a deposition in a couple of hours?

604
00:26:22,289 --> 00:26:24,457
- Yes.
- How are you feeling about it?

605
00:26:24,541 --> 00:26:26,543
Um, trying to think positively

606
00:26:26,627 --> 00:26:29,629
but feeling, um, less so.

607
00:26:29,713 --> 00:26:31,923
This job's really important
to me and my sister.

608
00:26:32,007 --> 00:26:33,557
You know, I support both of us.

609
00:26:33,592 --> 00:26:34,592
It's gonna go great.

610
00:26:34,635 --> 00:26:36,219
Just tell them what happened.

611
00:26:36,303 --> 00:26:37,804
You're not at fault.
Your job's not in jeopardy.

612
00:26:37,888 --> 00:26:39,889
I mean, the lawyers said that I could--

613
00:26:39,973 --> 00:26:42,058
The lawyers' job is to try
and shake your confidence.

614
00:26:42,142 --> 00:26:44,477
So don't let them.
You're a very good doctor.

615
00:26:44,561 --> 00:26:46,646
I have been training residents for years.

616
00:26:46,730 --> 00:26:49,357
You are one of the very best.

617
00:26:49,441 --> 00:26:50,650
I am?

618
00:26:50,734 --> 00:26:51,818
No, we need to stick to the plan.

619
00:26:51,902 --> 00:26:52,986
- I promise.
- Look.

620
00:26:53,070 --> 00:26:54,195
Thanks.

621
00:26:54,279 --> 00:26:55,530
She's not thinking clearly, okay?

622
00:26:55,614 --> 00:26:56,656
It's gonna be great.

623
00:26:56,740 --> 00:26:57,991
This is not what she wants.

624
00:26:58,075 --> 00:26:59,825
Then I'm taking her home.
That's it.

625
00:26:59,868 --> 00:27:01,828
We have to honor your wife's wishes.

626
00:27:01,912 --> 00:27:03,329
Even if she's loaded up on morphine

627
00:27:03,413 --> 00:27:05,165
- and can't think straight?
- Especially then.

628
00:27:05,249 --> 00:27:06,708
Hello.

629
00:27:06,792 --> 00:27:08,793
Paul Hamler, this is
my attending, Dr. Robinavitch.

630
00:27:08,877 --> 00:27:10,170
- Hi.
- Hi.

631
00:27:10,254 --> 00:27:12,672
Uh, my wife is not thinking clearly.

632
00:27:12,756 --> 00:27:15,216
What is it that she's asking for?

633
00:27:15,300 --> 00:27:17,469
Said she wants to stay here.

634
00:27:17,553 --> 00:27:19,513
Why don't we all go in and talk?

635
00:27:20,806 --> 00:27:22,766
Brian Jenkins is allowed to hunt with a .22

636
00:27:22,850 --> 00:27:24,225
on his grandpa's farm.

637
00:27:24,309 --> 00:27:26,269
Sounds like an accident
just waiting to happen.

638
00:27:26,353 --> 00:27:28,813
Mm-hmm.
And you're not Brian Jenkins.

639
00:27:28,897 --> 00:27:31,566
How are we doing in here, Roxie?

640
00:27:31,650 --> 00:27:33,193
Been better.

641
00:27:33,277 --> 00:27:34,819
Rumor has it you're still interested

642
00:27:34,903 --> 00:27:37,238
in booking a room with us?

643
00:27:37,322 --> 00:27:39,449
I don't wanna go back home yet.

644
00:27:39,533 --> 00:27:40,825
It's all set up, Rox.

645
00:27:40,909 --> 00:27:43,036
You're gonna be more comfortable at home.

646
00:27:43,120 --> 00:27:45,288
Paul, I changed my mind.

647
00:27:45,372 --> 00:27:46,748
It is our home.

648
00:27:48,709 --> 00:27:50,460
I don't--

649
00:27:50,544 --> 00:27:52,295
I don't want you living with my ghost.

650
00:27:52,379 --> 00:27:54,255
I will happily live with your ghost.

651
00:27:54,339 --> 00:27:57,842
Can we just all stop
talking about ghosts, please?

652
00:27:57,926 --> 00:27:59,052
Yes. I'm sorry.

653
00:27:59,136 --> 00:28:01,805
I'm sorry, sweetie.
You're right.

654
00:28:01,889 --> 00:28:03,839
Got trauma flying in.
ETA, five minutes.

655
00:28:03,891 --> 00:28:06,017
Okay.
Um, I'm very sorry.

656
00:28:06,101 --> 00:28:07,560
I will be right back.

657
00:28:07,644 --> 00:28:09,896
Excuse me.

658
00:28:09,980 --> 00:28:12,315
It's a boating accident,
swimmer versus propeller.

659
00:28:12,399 --> 00:28:13,650
Ouch.

660
00:28:13,734 --> 00:28:15,318
- What body parts involved?
- They didn't say.

661
00:28:15,402 --> 00:28:16,820
- How old?
- Nope.

662
00:28:16,904 --> 00:28:18,071
Anything?

663
00:28:18,155 --> 00:28:19,655
All I got was boating accident,

664
00:28:19,656 --> 00:28:22,006
- swimmer versus propeller.
- Propeller. Got it.

665
00:28:52,481 --> 00:28:55,775
Picked a hell of a day to come back, huh?

666
00:28:55,859 --> 00:28:58,736
How's Jake?

667
00:28:58,820 --> 00:29:00,446
He's good.

668
00:29:00,530 --> 00:29:02,615
He's better. He's coping.

669
00:29:02,699 --> 00:29:04,742
He's gonna be a senior this fall.

670
00:29:04,826 --> 00:29:07,162
That's great.

671
00:29:07,246 --> 00:29:10,331
That was a lot for him to go through.

672
00:29:10,415 --> 00:29:12,417
A lot for all of us to go through.

673
00:29:12,501 --> 00:29:13,919
Yeah.

674
00:29:15,545 --> 00:29:17,505
Okay, I'm just gonna say it!

675
00:29:17,589 --> 00:29:18,965
I'm sorry.

676
00:29:19,049 --> 00:29:20,592
I betrayed your trust.

677
00:29:20,676 --> 00:29:22,594
I betrayed our patients' trust.

678
00:29:22,678 --> 00:29:23,928
And I'm really fucking sorry.

679
00:29:24,012 --> 00:29:26,390
It'll never happen again,
I swear.

680
00:29:30,519 --> 00:29:34,314
I'm really glad that you
got the help that you need.

681
00:29:36,817 --> 00:29:40,737
But I don't know if
I want you working in my ER.

682
00:29:48,704 --> 00:29:49,913
Why'd you intubate him?

683
00:29:49,997 --> 00:29:51,289
He was splinting from the pain,

684
00:29:51,373 --> 00:29:52,874
barely moving air with sats in the 80s.

685
00:29:52,958 --> 00:29:54,250
How'd he get sliced up in the propeller?

686
00:29:54,334 --> 00:29:55,627
He was in the Allegheny

687
00:29:55,711 --> 00:29:57,045
trying to untangle a water ski tow line

688
00:29:57,129 --> 00:29:58,129
when his buddy started the engine.

689
00:29:58,213 --> 00:29:59,339
Drunk buddy, I assume?

690
00:29:59,423 --> 00:30:00,798
Well, it's 4th of July.
You tell me.

691
00:30:00,882 --> 00:30:02,175
Focus on the patient, please.

692
00:30:02,259 --> 00:30:04,303
Sofie, take over bagging.

693
00:30:06,305 --> 00:30:08,431
Okay. One, two, three.

694
00:30:08,515 --> 00:30:09,641
Watch that buckle.

695
00:30:10,934 --> 00:30:12,227
- Do you need me in here?
- Nope.

696
00:30:12,311 --> 00:30:14,938
We have a senior resident and an attending.

697
00:30:15,022 --> 00:30:16,231
Mel, can we start with a--

698
00:30:16,315 --> 00:30:18,816
- An EFAST? Sure.
- Yes, please.

699
00:30:18,900 --> 00:30:20,318
Why?

700
00:30:20,402 --> 00:30:21,778
To check and make sure
there's no pneumothorax.

701
00:30:21,862 --> 00:30:23,488
Otherwise, it could become a tension.

702
00:30:23,572 --> 00:30:26,115
Exactly. Oh, wow.

703
00:30:26,199 --> 00:30:28,368
- You want O-neg?
- Not without a BP first.

704
00:30:28,452 --> 00:30:31,412
108/64, pulse is 102.

705
00:30:31,496 --> 00:30:33,665
- Sats are good.
- Okay, let's have O-neg ready,

706
00:30:33,749 --> 00:30:36,835
- but don't give it just yet.
- Anything else?

707
00:30:39,087 --> 00:30:40,546
How about a hemocue?

708
00:30:40,630 --> 00:30:42,841
Uh, yeah.
Yeah, yeah, of course.

709
00:30:50,807 --> 00:30:52,601
Next step is fingernails.

710
00:30:54,394 --> 00:30:56,562
We'll go under each nail,

711
00:30:56,646 --> 00:31:01,025
first with the wet swab
and then with the dry one.

712
00:31:01,109 --> 00:31:03,569
Do you wanna take a break, hon?

713
00:31:03,653 --> 00:31:05,447
No.

714
00:31:08,325 --> 00:31:11,411
How much longer?

715
00:31:11,495 --> 00:31:13,295
After these, we'll get to external...

716
00:31:14,498 --> 00:31:16,416
And internal vaginal collection.

717
00:31:19,878 --> 00:31:23,506
It's the advocate from PAAR.

718
00:31:23,590 --> 00:31:25,174
They've been doing this longer than I have.

719
00:31:25,258 --> 00:31:27,558
They provide resources,
assistance, and support

720
00:31:27,636 --> 00:31:29,513
for sexual assault survivors.

721
00:31:31,681 --> 00:31:34,392
Hey.

722
00:31:34,476 --> 00:31:36,686
This will not define you, okay?

723
00:31:36,770 --> 00:31:40,523
You don't have to talk to them,
but I recommend you do.

724
00:31:40,607 --> 00:31:42,609
They're available 24/7.

725
00:31:44,361 --> 00:31:46,696
- Okay.
- Okay.

726
00:31:52,702 --> 00:31:54,287
Hi.

727
00:31:54,371 --> 00:31:56,622
I'm Paulette Sanderson from
Pittsburgh Action Against Rape.

728
00:31:56,706 --> 00:31:58,791
Hi, Paulette.
I'm the SANE, Dana.

729
00:31:58,875 --> 00:32:00,793
- And this is Ilana.
- Hello.

730
00:32:00,877 --> 00:32:03,296
I'm sorry to meet you
under these circumstances,

731
00:32:03,380 --> 00:32:05,465
but I and my organization
are here to help you navigate

732
00:32:05,549 --> 00:32:07,425
everything that comes next.

733
00:32:07,509 --> 00:32:10,511
I brought you some clothes
and basic necessities.

734
00:32:10,595 --> 00:32:12,138
I can even stay with you through the rest

735
00:32:12,222 --> 00:32:14,516
of your examination if you'd like.

736
00:32:16,601 --> 00:32:18,144
I don't think that's necessary.

737
00:32:18,228 --> 00:32:20,646
- Okay.
- That's fine.

738
00:32:20,730 --> 00:32:23,525
Would it be okay if
I asked you a few questions?

739
00:32:33,952 --> 00:32:35,203
Sure.

740
00:32:37,497 --> 00:32:40,917
Mm, our VRI isn't working.

741
00:32:41,001 --> 00:32:43,669
Video Relay Interpreter?

742
00:32:43,753 --> 00:32:45,253
Yeah, of course I rebooted it.

743
00:32:45,297 --> 00:32:46,881
Wait, how are you gonna
fix it if you don't know

744
00:32:46,965 --> 00:32:49,008
what the hell it is?

745
00:32:49,092 --> 00:32:51,177
Yeah, okay.
Whatever.

746
00:32:51,261 --> 00:32:53,221
I wanna do a head and belly scan on Harlow.

747
00:32:53,305 --> 00:32:54,514
Can you try telling her why?

748
00:32:54,598 --> 00:32:55,723
What about the VRI?

749
00:32:55,807 --> 00:32:57,600
It's DOA.

750
00:32:57,684 --> 00:33:00,603
I'm charting every free minute I get.

751
00:33:00,687 --> 00:33:02,438
I wasn't coming over for that.

752
00:33:02,522 --> 00:33:04,357
Good job in the Trauma earlier.

753
00:33:07,486 --> 00:33:08,528
What's this?

754
00:33:08,612 --> 00:33:09,737
Daniel Scott, 32,

755
00:33:09,821 --> 00:33:11,531
weak and dizzy while washing his car.

756
00:33:11,615 --> 00:33:14,033
Tachy at 106, BP 90/60.

757
00:33:14,117 --> 00:33:15,517
Temp's too high to register.

758
00:33:15,577 --> 00:33:17,120
We have a cooling room set up in North five.

759
00:33:17,204 --> 00:33:18,371
Okay, how are you feeling, Mr. Scott?

760
00:33:18,455 --> 00:33:19,539
Thirsty.

761
00:33:19,623 --> 00:33:20,915
Let's see if we can't fix that.

762
00:33:20,999 --> 00:33:22,875
He's gonna need a core temp, a CMP--whoa.

763
00:33:22,959 --> 00:33:24,459
Oh, hey, we need a trauma room.

764
00:33:24,503 --> 00:33:25,670
- What's open?
- Two.

765
00:33:25,754 --> 00:33:27,213
I'll grab the Ativan.

766
00:33:27,297 --> 00:33:28,897
- Any past medical history?
- No.

767
00:33:28,924 --> 00:33:30,716
Wife says he's healthy.
No meds, no allergies.

768
00:33:30,800 --> 00:33:33,553
He needs a core temp.

769
00:33:37,557 --> 00:33:39,058
Ready to transfer.

770
00:33:39,142 --> 00:33:40,351
Let's give two of Ativan.

771
00:33:40,435 --> 00:33:41,885
Don't want him seizing again.

772
00:33:41,895 --> 00:33:43,104
I gotta get back to my patients.

773
00:33:43,188 --> 00:33:44,105
Okay.

774
00:33:44,189 --> 00:33:46,858
One, two, three.

775
00:33:46,942 --> 00:33:47,900
Orders?

776
00:33:47,984 --> 00:33:50,027
Second IV with saline open.

777
00:33:50,111 --> 00:33:53,406
Sepsis panel, UA,
urine drug screen, EKG, and CK.

778
00:33:53,490 --> 00:33:55,492
I don't see any apparent trauma.

779
00:33:57,035 --> 00:33:59,745
- Pupils reactive.
- Mr. Scott? Daniel?

780
00:33:59,829 --> 00:34:01,289
Can you talk to me?

781
00:34:01,373 --> 00:34:03,040
Post-ictal, but moving all extremities.

782
00:34:03,124 --> 00:34:04,959
Pulse 137, BP 88/60.

783
00:34:05,043 --> 00:34:06,586
What are you thinking,
Dr. Santos?

784
00:34:06,670 --> 00:34:09,756
Uh, heat stroke,
but consider sepsis or drugs.

785
00:34:13,176 --> 00:34:16,512
Rectal temp is 104.6.

786
00:34:16,596 --> 00:34:18,646
All right, let's start with four ice packs

787
00:34:18,682 --> 00:34:20,391
on the groin and axilla.

788
00:34:20,475 --> 00:34:22,268
Should we do a full body ice bath?

789
00:34:22,352 --> 00:34:23,728
That'll take too long.
Do you have an Arctic Sun?

790
00:34:23,812 --> 00:34:25,104
Yeah, we do.

791
00:34:25,188 --> 00:34:26,772
Get pads on the chest,
abdomen, and both legs.

792
00:34:26,856 --> 00:34:28,483
I'll check back in.

793
00:34:30,026 --> 00:34:33,404
Ceftazidime is up, and first hemoglobin, 8.2.

794
00:34:33,488 --> 00:34:36,240
Eight is pretty low.
He must have bled down from 14.

795
00:34:36,324 --> 00:34:37,924
Anything you wanna do about that?

796
00:34:37,951 --> 00:34:40,870
Um, young, healthy guy.
We transfuse at seven.

797
00:34:40,954 --> 00:34:42,371
Do we?

798
00:34:42,455 --> 00:34:44,081
We'd be in real trouble if he equilibrates

799
00:34:44,165 --> 00:34:46,167
- from acute blood loss.
- Am I interrupting something?

800
00:34:46,251 --> 00:34:48,837
- Multiple deep lacerations--
- Motorboat versus--

801
00:34:51,506 --> 00:34:52,882
Jesus.

802
00:34:52,966 --> 00:34:54,550
This looks like some "Jurassic Park" shit.

803
00:34:54,634 --> 00:34:56,719
Is that your official surgical diagnosis?

804
00:34:56,803 --> 00:34:58,253
He is hemodynamically stable.

805
00:34:58,305 --> 00:35:00,556
What else do we know?

806
00:35:00,640 --> 00:35:04,310
Uh, intubated in the field
due to poor tidal volume.

807
00:35:04,394 --> 00:35:06,562
EFAST was negative for pneumothorax,

808
00:35:06,646 --> 00:35:09,065
so no need to do a chest tube.

809
00:35:09,149 --> 00:35:11,734
And no free fluid in the abdomen,

810
00:35:11,818 --> 00:35:13,569
good hemostasis inside the wounds.

811
00:35:13,653 --> 00:35:14,946
Nothing arterial.

812
00:35:15,030 --> 00:35:16,697
At first, he had a hemoglobin of 8.2.

813
00:35:16,781 --> 00:35:18,199
We'll follow that closely.

814
00:35:18,283 --> 00:35:21,036
With no active bleeding,
I wouldn't transfuse just yet.

815
00:35:23,288 --> 00:35:25,122
Dr. Langdon agrees with you.

816
00:35:25,206 --> 00:35:27,291
Let's get him to CT.

817
00:35:27,375 --> 00:35:29,710
Jason Stills, 62, was gathering the makings

818
00:35:29,794 --> 00:35:32,494
of a salad when he started
feeling dizzy and nauseated.

819
00:35:32,547 --> 00:35:33,673
Vomited once.

820
00:35:33,757 --> 00:35:34,924
How are you feeling,
Mr. Stills?

821
00:35:35,008 --> 00:35:36,592
Like I'm gonna die.

822
00:35:36,676 --> 00:35:38,636
Well, you came to the right
place to prevent that.

823
00:35:38,720 --> 00:35:40,721
Do you mind if I touch your abdomen?

824
00:35:40,805 --> 00:35:42,890
- Yeah, sure.
- Okay.

825
00:35:42,974 --> 00:35:45,226
- Does this hurt at all?
- No.

826
00:35:45,310 --> 00:35:48,479
He's tachycardic at 124 with a temp of 102.4.

827
00:35:48,563 --> 00:35:50,481
Hey, Joy, what's your suggestion?

828
00:35:50,565 --> 00:35:52,149
Keep hydrating, check electrolytes,

829
00:35:52,233 --> 00:35:53,359
and move him to the cooling room.

830
00:35:53,443 --> 00:35:54,569
Precisely.

831
00:35:54,653 --> 00:35:55,778
Good luck finding a parking spot.

832
00:35:55,862 --> 00:35:58,823
- North five.
- What? No valet?

833
00:36:02,952 --> 00:36:04,620
Jada. Hey.

834
00:36:04,704 --> 00:36:06,831
I--I've been looking all over for you.

835
00:36:06,915 --> 00:36:08,332
I just went for a walk.

836
00:36:08,416 --> 00:36:11,503
I wanted to talk to you, if that's okay.

837
00:36:13,338 --> 00:36:15,089
So does Dr. Jefferson.

838
00:36:15,173 --> 00:36:17,508
It's important that you get
to hear what he has to say.

839
00:36:17,592 --> 00:36:18,801
Why?

840
00:36:18,885 --> 00:36:20,886
He doesn't want me to go crazy
like my brother?

841
00:36:20,970 --> 00:36:23,764
Or kill myself like my uncle?

842
00:36:23,848 --> 00:36:25,808
Of course not.

843
00:36:25,892 --> 00:36:28,728
We--we still have no idea
what caused Jackson's episode.

844
00:36:28,812 --> 00:36:31,439
Episode.

845
00:36:31,523 --> 00:36:33,566
Right.

846
00:36:33,650 --> 00:36:37,820
- Look, I--
- I know this must be so scary for you.

847
00:36:37,904 --> 00:36:41,365
And you probably feel
betrayed by your parents.

848
00:36:41,449 --> 00:36:44,243
But they had no way of knowing about Jackson.

849
00:36:44,327 --> 00:36:46,621
You know, and some families
just have a difficult time

850
00:36:46,705 --> 00:36:50,041
talking about mental health.

851
00:36:50,125 --> 00:36:52,084
Now you can help us take the first steps

852
00:36:52,168 --> 00:36:55,547
to finding out what we can
do to help your brother.

853
00:37:00,635 --> 00:37:05,973
Mr. Diaz,
I have a surprise for you.

854
00:37:06,057 --> 00:37:07,808
Oh.

855
00:37:07,892 --> 00:37:09,060
Sorry.

856
00:37:09,144 --> 00:37:10,478
It's okay.

857
00:37:10,562 --> 00:37:12,313
Have you--have you seen my patient?

858
00:37:12,397 --> 00:37:15,066
Orlando? Mr. Diaz?

859
00:37:15,150 --> 00:37:17,401
Room was empty.

860
00:37:17,485 --> 00:37:20,405
- Seriously?
- Yeah.

861
00:37:24,951 --> 00:37:26,577
What happened to you?

862
00:37:26,661 --> 00:37:28,454
Oh.

863
00:37:28,538 --> 00:37:29,872
Bullet grazed my vest.

864
00:37:29,956 --> 00:37:31,082
You were shot?

865
00:37:31,166 --> 00:37:32,750
Shot at.

866
00:37:32,834 --> 00:37:35,961
Geniuses thought today was the
day to rob a goods warehouse.

867
00:37:36,045 --> 00:37:37,254
Didn't think about how long it would take

868
00:37:37,338 --> 00:37:38,631
to load the appliances.

869
00:37:38,715 --> 00:37:39,924
They panicked.

870
00:37:40,008 --> 00:37:41,217
All hell broke loose.

871
00:37:41,301 --> 00:37:43,011
Jesus.

872
00:37:45,346 --> 00:37:47,223
Why do you do this?

873
00:37:47,307 --> 00:37:49,392
My therapist said
I needed a hobby.

874
00:37:49,476 --> 00:37:50,976
Funny.

875
00:37:51,060 --> 00:37:53,062
Shit.

876
00:37:53,146 --> 00:37:55,231
This--this sucks.

877
00:37:55,315 --> 00:37:56,899
- Oh, it's nothing.
- No.

878
00:37:56,983 --> 00:37:59,318
No, don't worry about me.
I'm fine. Seriously.

879
00:37:59,402 --> 00:38:00,569
No, my patient.

880
00:38:00,653 --> 00:38:02,238
He didn't have any insurance,

881
00:38:02,322 --> 00:38:06,575
and he was already
in a mountain of medical debt.

882
00:38:06,659 --> 00:38:08,536
He couldn't afford any of his meds.

883
00:38:08,620 --> 00:38:10,871
Hmm.

884
00:38:10,955 --> 00:38:12,289
What's in the bag?

885
00:38:12,373 --> 00:38:17,253
Insulin, test strips, electrolyte powder.

886
00:38:17,337 --> 00:38:20,047
I--I got him everything
he needed for home care.

887
00:38:20,131 --> 00:38:22,258
So Uber it to his house.

888
00:38:22,342 --> 00:38:24,677
Is the hospital gonna pay for that?

889
00:38:24,761 --> 00:38:26,888
I'll pay for it.

890
00:38:36,981 --> 00:38:38,941
What are you doing?

891
00:38:39,025 --> 00:38:41,569
What you clearly can't.

892
00:38:41,653 --> 00:38:43,362
Did you make a chart?

893
00:38:43,446 --> 00:38:44,655
No.

894
00:38:44,739 --> 00:38:46,240
This can stay off the books.

895
00:38:46,324 --> 00:38:48,242
Don't need the paperwork from the hospital

896
00:38:48,326 --> 00:38:50,077
or the police department.

897
00:38:50,161 --> 00:38:52,163
Okay.

898
00:38:52,247 --> 00:38:53,873
Our little secret.

899
00:38:57,252 --> 00:38:59,712
How's he doing?
Any more seizures?

900
00:38:59,796 --> 00:39:00,838
Nope.

901
00:39:00,922 --> 00:39:02,131
Temp 102.9.

902
00:39:02,215 --> 00:39:03,424
Labs back?

903
00:39:03,508 --> 00:39:05,050
Mostly signs of dehydration.

904
00:39:05,134 --> 00:39:08,763
A tad hypernatremic,
mild BUN and creatinine bump.

905
00:39:08,847 --> 00:39:11,348
CK 400 something--
Nothing worrisome yet.

906
00:39:11,432 --> 00:39:12,892
Okay, good. Keep cooling.

907
00:39:12,976 --> 00:39:14,894
- I'll monitor him.
- Great.

908
00:39:14,978 --> 00:39:18,064
That'll give Dr. Santos
a chance to get caught up.

909
00:39:21,401 --> 00:39:24,028
Your R2 year can be challenging.

910
00:39:24,112 --> 00:39:26,864
You just have to keep grinding.

911
00:39:26,948 --> 00:39:29,033
What's your dispo plan for Mr. Scott?

912
00:39:29,117 --> 00:39:30,868
Uh, ICU admission.

913
00:39:30,952 --> 00:39:33,037
You should call Neurology to consult.

914
00:39:33,121 --> 00:39:34,580
Yeah, done.

915
00:39:34,664 --> 00:39:37,041
Since it was exertional heat
illness in a young person,

916
00:39:37,125 --> 00:39:38,751
the mortality is low.

917
00:39:38,835 --> 00:39:41,712
But non-exertional heatstroke
in an elderly person,

918
00:39:41,796 --> 00:39:43,756
- you need to worry.
- Okay.

919
00:39:43,840 --> 00:39:46,842
I'll put in orders for repeat labs.

920
00:39:46,926 --> 00:39:48,887
Good work in there.

921
00:40:01,774 --> 00:40:05,778
This 49-year-old woman presents
to the emergency department--

922
00:40:08,990 --> 00:40:13,619
Uh, with the chief complaint
of right ear pain.

923
00:40:13,703 --> 00:40:16,413
Hey, Donnie, can you do something about that?

924
00:40:16,497 --> 00:40:17,832
What?

925
00:40:17,916 --> 00:40:19,333
Seriously?

926
00:40:19,417 --> 00:40:21,168
That--that's not driving you nuts?

927
00:40:21,252 --> 00:40:23,212
The baby, it won't stop crying.

928
00:40:23,296 --> 00:40:25,297
Oh, that?
It's music to my ears now.

929
00:40:25,381 --> 00:40:26,681
I think Jesse's the nurse.

930
00:40:26,758 --> 00:40:29,385
Well, can't you--ugh.

931
00:40:35,516 --> 00:40:36,768
Fuck.

932
00:40:41,814 --> 00:40:44,191
What the hell is going on?

933
00:40:44,275 --> 00:40:46,402
With what?

934
00:40:46,486 --> 00:40:49,405
With her.
Can't you make her stop crying?

935
00:40:49,489 --> 00:40:52,575
She's been fed and changed.
She's cranky from rhinovirus.

936
00:40:54,202 --> 00:40:56,495
Isn't there something that you can do?

937
00:40:56,579 --> 00:40:59,123
She's due for her next Tylenol.

938
00:40:59,207 --> 00:41:00,499
Give me a minute.
I'll be right back.

939
00:41:00,583 --> 00:41:02,752
Wait, no, no, no,
I'm not gonna stay here.

940
00:41:05,546 --> 00:41:07,548
What is your problem?

941
00:41:10,259 --> 00:41:14,597
This is precisely why
I didn't go into Pedes.

942
00:41:14,681 --> 00:41:15,806
Okay.

943
00:41:15,890 --> 00:41:17,641
Hey, hey.

944
00:41:17,725 --> 00:41:20,770
Hey, little Miss Sunshine.

945
00:41:22,271 --> 00:41:24,607
Is it time for you to take a little nap?

946
00:41:24,691 --> 00:41:26,775
That would be so fucking nice.

947
00:41:26,859 --> 00:41:28,111
Yes, it would.

948
00:41:31,322 --> 00:41:34,491
I'm starting to understand
why you got left here.

949
00:41:34,575 --> 00:41:36,744
Hey, shh.

950
00:42:22,999 --> 00:42:24,541
What's the word from CT?

951
00:42:24,625 --> 00:42:27,544
Nothing intrathoracic,
nothing intra-abdominal.

952
00:42:27,628 --> 00:42:29,004
Propeller just missed gutting him.

953
00:42:29,088 --> 00:42:30,422
- Very fortunate.
- Okay.

954
00:42:30,506 --> 00:42:32,341
Repeat hemoglobin is eight.

955
00:42:32,425 --> 00:42:35,052
We're holding off on transfusing.

956
00:42:35,136 --> 00:42:36,637
Plan?

957
00:42:36,721 --> 00:42:38,806
I'll have Mel and Langdon
suture up the lacerations.

958
00:42:38,890 --> 00:42:41,058
Wait, what?
That could take days.

959
00:42:41,142 --> 00:42:42,351
I--I can't--

960
00:42:42,435 --> 00:42:44,311
Calm down, Sadness.
I'm kidding.

961
00:42:44,395 --> 00:42:46,897
This is one for my skilled
surgical residents upstairs,

962
00:42:46,981 --> 00:42:48,399
not you Boy Scout butchers.

963
00:42:48,483 --> 00:42:49,775
Boy, I missed you, Yoyo.

964
00:42:49,859 --> 00:42:52,027
Mm. Can't say the same.

965
00:42:52,111 --> 00:42:55,572
Okay, let's take up this art project.

966
00:42:55,656 --> 00:42:56,907
So about before--

967
00:42:56,991 --> 00:42:58,951
Back to it.

968
00:42:59,035 --> 00:43:00,369
Good talk.

969
00:43:00,453 --> 00:43:01,870
How we doing, Princess?

970
00:43:01,954 --> 00:43:03,455
All right.
A little bloated.

971
00:43:03,539 --> 00:43:06,917
I had one too many hot dogs from the truck.

972
00:43:07,001 --> 00:43:08,961
You meant the board, huh?

973
00:43:09,045 --> 00:43:12,089
Gus, our incarcerated patient,
got a spot upstairs.

974
00:43:12,173 --> 00:43:15,718
Looking for our unhoused
patient, Digby, and, of course,

975
00:43:15,802 --> 00:43:18,595
we have Whitaker, Donahue,
and the med students

976
00:43:18,679 --> 00:43:21,329
on these diversion intakes,
but they just keep coming.

977
00:43:21,349 --> 00:43:23,225
Yeah, we may need to start
just sending people up

978
00:43:23,309 --> 00:43:25,561
and ask for forgiveness
instead of permission.

979
00:43:25,645 --> 00:43:28,063
Hello?

980
00:43:28,147 --> 00:43:30,357
Oh, okay.

981
00:43:30,441 --> 00:43:32,609
Yes, I will be right there.

982
00:43:32,693 --> 00:43:34,194
C-suite wants to see me upstairs.

983
00:43:34,278 --> 00:43:35,571
Ooh, called to the principal's office

984
00:43:35,655 --> 00:43:38,824
on your first day--
Not a good sign.

985
00:43:38,908 --> 00:43:41,410
- I think I'm a baby whisperer.
- Hey, great.

986
00:43:41,494 --> 00:43:43,694
We'll add Baby Jane Doe to your patient load.

987
00:43:43,704 --> 00:43:45,080
Forget I said anything.

988
00:43:45,164 --> 00:43:46,957
Where are we with your deaf patient, Harlow?

989
00:43:47,041 --> 00:43:50,586
Uh, the VRI was a bust, but
the interpreter's on the way.

990
00:43:50,670 --> 00:43:52,546
Figured I'd just give her
a head and belly scan

991
00:43:52,630 --> 00:43:54,757
- and go from there.
- No, wait for the interpreter.

992
00:43:54,841 --> 00:43:57,291
No need to give the patient
unnecessary radiation.

993
00:43:57,343 --> 00:43:59,636
And your charting?

994
00:43:59,720 --> 00:44:01,096
Catching up and checking it twice.

995
00:44:01,180 --> 00:44:02,556
Good.

996
00:44:02,640 --> 00:44:04,975
Hey, have you had a chance
to speak to Langdon today?

997
00:44:05,059 --> 00:44:06,769
Uh, no.

998
00:44:06,853 --> 00:44:08,062
Why? Did he say something?

999
00:44:08,146 --> 00:44:09,688
No, just curious.

1000
00:44:09,772 --> 00:44:13,067
How is everything at home
with you and Whitaker?

1001
00:44:13,151 --> 00:44:15,444
He's weirder than you'd expect.

1002
00:44:15,528 --> 00:44:17,237
- Hmm.
- Yeah.

1003
00:44:17,321 --> 00:44:19,323
But I don't see him all that much.

1004
00:44:19,407 --> 00:44:21,007
He spends a lot of time at Amy's.

1005
00:44:21,033 --> 00:44:23,327
He has a girlfriend?

1006
00:44:23,411 --> 00:44:27,122
I don't know what to call it.

1007
00:44:27,206 --> 00:44:29,666
The--the farmer who got burned last year

1008
00:44:29,750 --> 00:44:32,252
the day of the mass cas, his widow, Amy.

1009
00:44:32,336 --> 00:44:33,545
Oh, he died?

1010
00:44:33,629 --> 00:44:35,589
Yeah, he had burns on 90% of his body.

1011
00:44:35,673 --> 00:44:37,473
His chance of survival was very slim.

1012
00:44:37,550 --> 00:44:39,051
Okay, so I'm an optimist.

1013
00:44:39,135 --> 00:44:41,637
The sun doesn't always
come out tomorrow, Annie.

1014
00:44:41,721 --> 00:44:43,514
Wait, wasn't she pregnant?

1015
00:44:43,598 --> 00:44:46,183
No, she was a young orphan.

1016
00:44:46,267 --> 00:44:48,519
No, not Annie. Amy.

1017
00:44:48,603 --> 00:44:52,231
Yes.
Yes, very pregnant and young.

1018
00:44:52,315 --> 00:44:54,191
Whitaker is now seeing this Amy?

1019
00:44:54,275 --> 00:44:56,235
And her baby.

1020
00:44:56,319 --> 00:44:58,070
He got really close to the family

1021
00:44:58,154 --> 00:44:59,905
when the husband was dying.

1022
00:44:59,989 --> 00:45:02,074
He really believed that
the guy would pull through.

1023
00:45:02,158 --> 00:45:04,576
He helped her through
the loss of her husband,

1024
00:45:04,660 --> 00:45:06,203
and then again when she had the kid,

1025
00:45:06,287 --> 00:45:09,540
and now he spends almost
every weekend at the farm.

1026
00:45:09,624 --> 00:45:10,791
Huh.

1027
00:45:10,875 --> 00:45:12,325
Plus, he's on the street team,

1028
00:45:12,335 --> 00:45:14,085
and he just wants to help everybody.

1029
00:45:14,128 --> 00:45:17,172
And I just don't wanna see him
taken advantage of, you know?

1030
00:45:17,256 --> 00:45:19,341
He's just a fucking Huckleberry.

1031
00:45:19,425 --> 00:45:22,094
Yeah, but he's our fucking Huckleberry.

1032
00:45:22,178 --> 00:45:23,595
I'll talk to him.

1033
00:45:23,679 --> 00:45:24,805
Hey, your call.

1034
00:45:24,889 --> 00:45:26,723
Strong deflection.
Well played.

1035
00:45:26,807 --> 00:45:28,058
You're the boss.

1036
00:45:28,142 --> 00:45:29,768
Or you are until end of shift today.

1037
00:45:29,852 --> 00:45:30,978
Still the boss.

1038
